<worksheet xml:id="ws-negative-binomial">
    <title>The Negative Binomial Distribution (2.5)</title>
<page>
    <exercise workspace="3in">
      <statement>
        <p>
           The world series in baseball is a seven game series between an
            American League (AL) team and a National League team (NL) where the
            winner is the first team that wins <m>4</m> games. Suppose the
            probability that the AL team wins any given game is <m>p=0.55</m>.
            In other words, for the sake of this problem, whether a team wins a
            game is independent of the wins in the other games. What is the
            probability that the AL team wins in <m>6</m> games?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>  
    <exercise workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Jerry is selling life insurance over the phone. The probability that
            any given call will result in a sale is <m>0.25</m>. Find the
            probability that his <m>2^{nd}</m> sale happens on his <m>5^{th}</m> call.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
</page>

<page>

<definition xml:id="negative-binomial">
  <title>Negative Binomial Distribution</title>
  <statement>
    <p>Suppose a sequence of independent Bernoulli trials is repeated
      (each with probability <m>p</m> of success) and let the random variable
      <m>X</m> denote the trial on which the <m>r^{th}</m> success occurs. Then we
      say <m>X</m> has a <em>negative binomial</em> distribution.
    </p>
  </statement>
</definition>
  
<exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Suppose <m>X</m> has a negative binomial distribution. 
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace="2in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the pmf of <m>X</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
 <task workspace="1in">
  <statement>
    <p>
      The mean and variance of <m>X</m> are given by:
    </p>
  </statement>
  </task>
</exercise>
<exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      A fair six-sided die is rolled repeatedly.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        What is the probability that the <m>5</m> appears for the
                  <m>3^{rd}</m> time on the <m>15^{th} </m> roll of the die?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        What is the probability that the first <m>5</m> appears
                  sometime after the fourth roll?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        How many rolls to you expect before you get the <m>6^{th}</m> five?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
<exercise workspace="6in">
<statement>
  <p>
    A fair six-sided die is rolled until each face is observed at
                  least once. On average, how many rolls are needed?
  </p>
</statement>           
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The probability that any customer at Starbucks orders the new holiday latte is 0.45. What is the probability that the fourth holiday latte is sold to the <m>10^{th}</m> customer? (Assume independence, and that each customer only buys one drink.)
      </p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The probability that Joe wakes up before his alarm goes off while he is on vacation is <m>0.35</m>. What is the probability that the second time he wakes up before his alarm goes off is the <m>5^{th}</m> day of Joe's vacation?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        The probability that a baseball team wins a game is <m>0.6</m> (assume independence). 
      </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          What is the probability that the first game they win is the <m>3^{rd}</m> game of the season?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          What is the probability that they win their <m>2^{nd}</m> game within their first <m>4</m> games?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Once a team wins <m>15</m> games, they are guaranteed to be in the championship tournament. Once they win their <m>15^{th}</m> game, they are said to <q>make the tournament</q>. What is the expected number of games the team must play before they make the tournament?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>
</page>
</worksheet>